---
import Icon from "./Icon.astro"
import SystemMap from "./SystemMap.astro"
import RemoteSetup from "./RemoteSetup.astro"
---
<section id="controls" class="system-section" aria-labelledby="controls-title">
  <h2 id="controls-title" class="sr-only">System map and automatic recovery</h2>
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div><p>Automatic operation. Manual controls when you need them.</p></div>
    <div class="heading-actions">
      <button class="button" id="start-system" type="button" disabled><Icon name="play" size={16} />Start system</button>
      <button class="button button-danger" id="stop-remote" type="button" disabled><Icon name="power" size={16} />Shut down VPS…</button>
      <button class="button button-danger" id="stop-system" type="button" disabled><Icon name="power" size={16} />Shut down system…</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <RemoteSetup />
  <SystemMap />
  <p id="shutdown-detail" class="control-detail">System shutdown keeps this dashboard and the recovery supervisor running. Your PC is never powered off.</p>
  <article class="panel control-panel auth-panel">
      <div class="control-heading"><h3>ChatGPT sign-in</h3><span id="auth-state" class="status-pill neutral">Checking…</span></div>
      <p id="auth-countdown" class="auth-countdown">—</p>
      <p id="auth-deadline" class="control-detail">Reading local authentication metadata…</p>
      <p class="control-detail">This is the access token’s expiry, not a usage-limit reset. OpenCode may refresh it automatically.</p>
      <p class="control-detail">If sign-in is required, use OpenCode’s Connect provider flow. This page never refreshes tokens or makes model requests.</p>
  </article>
  <div id="control-notice" class="notice" role="status" hidden></div>
</section>
